package server

const mcpCollaborationDocumentPolicy = "Bridge 0.8.0 advertises collaboration-document-v1 for portable schemaVersion:1 diagram.collaboration profiles, comments, tasks and informational activity, separately from realtime collaboration-v1. GET /diagrams/{diagramId}/collaboration/document returns {diagramId,baseVersion,document}; absent work returns an empty version-1 document. POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/collaboration/actions takes exactly {baseVersion,action} and returns Graph. No queries, hashes or extra body fields are accepted. Supported action.type values: profile.create/update/remove, comment.create/reply/edit/remove/resolve, task.create/update/remove. Read the exact endpoint schema before writing. Full graph PUT inherits omitted document work and rejects explicitly changed collaboration payloads; Diagram PATCH cannot write this namespace. Use the typed actions for existing work. Actors, role, source, IDs and writer-clock timestamps are supplied by the browser adapter, never request authorId/profileId/role/timestamp/source/device credentials. Local document work needs no relay; writes require Read + write and viewers cannot mutate. Owner provisions/deletes profiles, editors update only their own display profile, comment authors edit only their own text, owner may delete for moderation, thread author/owner resolves or reopens, and editors assign/update node tasks. Profiles are unverified display labels with stable UUIDs, separate from process responsibility Owner records and private live-device identity. Creation with omitted/null color picks the first unused eight-color palette entry, then balances reuse; names/initials also distinguish participants. Tasks use todo|in-progress|done, optional assigneeId and valid YYYY-MM-DD dueDate; nullable optional avatarDataUrl/description/assigneeId/dueDate clears the field, and profile update color:null clears its explicit color. Node/profile references are validated; deleted-node work retains its UUID and last title. Referenced profiles cannot be deleted. Stale baseVersion returns 409, role/author violations 403, invalid action/schema 422 and missing targets 404; existing locked-workspace/grant/browser errors remain. Limits are 128 profiles, 2000 threads/messages total, 1000 tasks, 500 activity entries, 4000 UTF-16 code units per comment/description, 4 million total comment code units, 64 KiB decoded per avatar and 2 MiB combined, 256 by 256 pixels maximum for PNG/JPEG/WebP, and 16 MiB UTF-8 document data. SVG/external/animated PNG/WebP avatars are rejected; UI decode/re-encodes uploads. Native JSON and backups preserve document work and remap node references. Comment messages and activity use logical sequence with UUID ties, independent of clock skew. Activity retains the latest 500 events by that order, skips camera/layout noise and uses writer-clock values. It is informational editable content, not a signed or immutable security audit. The current shared CRDT trusts approved editors to edit document content; action ownership checks do not claim cryptographic authorship provenance."
